    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Hyliion has decisively pivoted from its legacy hybrid truck powertrain business to become a stationary power-generation play centered on the KARNO generator. The fuel-agnostic linear generator, originally acquired from GE, is now targeting two substantial end-markets: AI data centers facing urgent power constraints and defense applications validated by a DARPA-backed U.S. Navy trial on an unmanned vessel. The technology’s ability to run on natural gas, hydrogen, or diesel on the same hardware broadens its addressable use cases. Market attention has shifted sharply toward this modular, scalable power solution as the core driver of Hyliion’s renewed relevance.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership, spearheaded by CEO Thomas Healy, has repositioned the company as a critical “power layer” for AI infrastructure, departing entirely from commercial vehicle electrification. The strategy involves securing early commercial interest through letters of intent while advancing toward year-end commercialization of the KARNO power module. The successful lab demonstration of multi-fuel capability and the Navy trial award have bolstered credibility with the market, as reflected in recent analyst initiations with bullish ratings. Management is actively communicating this strategic vision via public webcasts, aiming to sustain momentum through tangible execution milestones.",
